^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Alignment attributes of declarations apply to the declared entity; for members
they can only increase its alignment, whereas those of typedefs and struct
definitions are the alignment of the type, which packing overrides. GCC applies
attributes following the '*' of a pointer declarator to the pointer type.
